  "description": "Document 113 event contract for the events app/modules/validation/commands_integrity.py actually emits. 1 of the catalogue's 4 declared Document 89 events is directly named-matched (DataIntegrityQualificationApproved); the other 3 exist under a dict-keyed lookup this catalogue's own event_type= grep would miss: AuditTamperTestCompleted (the default outcome for reorder/delete/edit/overwrite tamper actions), VaultCanonicalizationVerified and ArchiveRetrievalVerified (both keyed off `tamper_action` in `_EVENT_BY_ACTION`). All 4 of the catalogue's declared events are therefore implemented. (The module also emits an undeclared DataIntegrityProfileDefined at profile-authoring time -- not part of the catalogue's declared 4.) Verified directly against source, including indirection through the shared finalize() helper and, where present, dict-keyed event-type lookups and parameterized shared helpers -- not a literal-string grep alone.",
